      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "To a solution of DyCl3·6H2O (0.75 mmol) and 2-nitrophenol (2-NP, 0.25 mmol) in MeOH (15 mL) was added a solution of H2hmb (1.0 mmol) and triethylamine (2.25 mmol) in MeOH (15 mL). The resulting orange solution gave well-formed dark red crystals by vapor diffusion of diethyl ether into the mother liquor over one week at ambient temperature. The crystals are a 50:50 disordered pair of [Dy3(Hhmb)4(μ3-OMe)2(OMe)(2-NP)]+ and [Dy3(Hhmb)4(μ3-OMe)2(2-NP)]+ with three chloride counterions.",
