      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Trinuclear Dy(III) SMM. Room-temperature χMT is close to the value for three uncoupled Dy(III) ions and decreases on cooling, consistent with weak antiferromagnetic interactions and/or anisotropy. Under zero dc field, complex 1 shows frequency-dependent out-of-phase susceptibility with an effective barrier of 12.18 K. A small applied dc field has little effect, so zero-field QTM is not efficient. The low barrier is attributed to noncoplanar anisotropy axes rather than a toroidal SMT arrangement.",
